17","event_uuid":"7cc077d7-488d-48f5-ba40-3a0e881d27e6","position":{"commit_sha":"f10c42b540bd9dadd4ae06c390f051d5909c8fbd","position":"1794443798366571188-7cc077d7-488d-48f5-ba40-3a0e881d27e6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"07841f97f4443e2fc2439570ddcbd28d78898467151331365fec639fd738681d","event_uuid":"0f30d73f-2551-444a-bbbb-a32b40d95687","position":{"commit_sha":"3d33da3f3772e3e7e5be1b2df070d70443458339","position":"1794443861179355776-0f30d73f-2551-444a-bbbb-a32b40d95687"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation note: pinning `runs-on: ubuntu-26.04` trips `make lint` because actionlint 1.7.12 (the pinned version and the latest release) does not know the label (`label \"ubuntu-26.04\" is unknown [runner-label]`). The label is GitHub-hosted GA; the upstream gap is rhysd/actionlint#682. Added `.github/actionlint.yaml` declaring only `ubuntu-26.04`, the documented workaround, so the label check stays on for every other runner name. File impact updated.","timestamp":1794372492858406070},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 3353 (patch set 1, 240b26b74e9). `make verify` passed before push: exit 0, 20,922 default-tier and 202 integration-tier tests passed. The new tests were also run against the unfixed code; all 9 new or updated assertions failed there and pass on the fix.","timestamp":1794440687604375717},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 3353 merged at LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved; merge commit c80576dfdb390411d45183afd0cdaffcbb56cd12. Pre-merge Verified run 43121915726 used main's workflow (waiver still in env, as plan review noted), but the patchset's gate code ran on ubuntu-26.04 and its summary recorded `\"sandbox\": \"bwrap\"`. Post-merge proof: dispatched Mutation Testing Sweep run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/43125887080 on main at c80576dfdb3; result pending.","timestamp":1794442523945812620},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Post-merge proof: Mutation Testing Sweep run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/43125887080 on main at c80576dfdb3 concluded success, all 7 shards. Shard logs (e.g. jobs 130877924099 next-batch, 130877924332 signing) show `Image: ubuntu-26.04`, no `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` in step env, no namespace warning, no UNSANDBOXED line, and `\"sandbox\": \"bwrap\"` in summary.json. All acceptance criteria met; boxes ticked.","timestamp":1794443764347870512},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE (2026-11-11 PST): Fix merged as Gerrit change 3353, merge commit c80576dfdb390411d45183afd0cdaffcbb56cd12. Post-merge sweep https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/43125887080 succeeded on ubuntu-26.04 with `\"sandbox\": \"bwrap\"` and no waiver. All AC boxes are ticked. Ticket is still in_progress. Completion verifier job 1794443782493530018-579c2394de9c487dbe09af951c0b0a86 (ref c80576dfdb3) was running when this session handed off. Next: poll verify_completion_status; once certified, transition in_progress -> closed with close_class preexisting. Worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-aurochs is at c80576dfdb3 with make install done. Plan-review status reads stale-code; that is expected after implementation.","timestamp":1794443798366571188}],"created_at":1794262554720512001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"19f5a89d-a33e-4fd5-936b-8ee2be755b11","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f86a-c0ce-f107-405f"},{"link_uuid":"748466f6-ffd4-42cc-819e-70ea7bd789de","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e5df-89bd-7e75-4031"}],"description":"## Observation\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml:203` (origin/main 9f8b2af21c8) sets `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED: \"1\"` unconditionally on the `Run mutation shard` step of the `bounded mutation gate` job (`runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, line 127). Comments at lines 92-94, 187-189 and 197-199 justify it with \"Hosted Ubuntu denies unprivileged CLONE_NEWUSER\".\n- Run 41939410124 (change 3328, 2026-11-04 PST), job 126957533578, `Image: ubuntu-24.04`: step env shows the waiver, then `bwrap is installed but cannot create a namespace (bwrap: setting up uid map: Permission denied)` and `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED is set: running mutation tests UNSANDBOXED`. All 7 shards concluded `success`. `summary.json` (`scripts/mutation_gate.py` `run_gate`, lines 698-745) has no sandbox field, so a waived pass and a sandboxed pass produce identical evidence and the same Verified vote.\n- Run 42949111146 (2026-11-10 PST), job 130289932461, `Image: ubuntu-26.04`, `bubblewrap 0.11.1`: no namespace warning, no waiver line, `\"outcome\": \"success\"`. Why 26.04 permits the namespace (image AppArmor userns policy) is not established; it is an observed property of that image. `ubuntu-latest` is mid-migration from 24.04 to 26.04, so a floating label can still land on 24.04.\n\n## Root cause\nThe workflow pre-sets the operator waiver, so `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py` `wrap()` (lines 201-224) takes its `opt_out_enabled(env)` branch and returns argv unwrapped whenever `probe()` finds no working mechanism, instead of raising `SandboxUnavailable`. Separately, `mutation_gate.main()` (line 777) catches only `GateError`, so a raised `SandboxUnavailable` would crash with a traceback and write no `summary.json`.\n\n## Impact\nOn a runner where bwrap cannot create a namespace, mutated code runs with write access to the whole runner and the gate still reports green as though sandboxed. The 2026-08-26 destructive-mutation incident (`e668-b496-e264-4283`) is the hazard the sandbox exists for.\n\n## Approach\n1. `_mutation.yml`: delete the waiver env line; pin the `bounded mutation gate` job to `runs-on: ubuntu-26.04`, the image observed to start bwrap, so availability does not depend on where the floating label points; rewrite the three stale comments to say the lane fails closed when bwrap cannot start. Rationale: the waiver no longer buys availability on 26.04 and only removes protection. Back-out if a future 26.04 image regresses: the lane goes red with `failure_class: sandbox-unavailable`; fix the runner (image or AppArmor), never re-add the waiver.\n2. `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py`: add `UNSANDBOXED = \"unsandboxed\"` and `mechanism(env) -> str`, returning `probe()`'s result, or `UNSANDBOXED` when the operator waiver is set, or raising `SandboxUnavailable`. `wrap()` calls it, so wrapping behaviour is unchanged. The local operator waiver stays (documented in `docs/local-dev-env.md`); no config key, env var or feature flag is added.\n3. `scripts/mutation_gate.py`: `run_gate` calls `mutation_sandbox.mechanism()` once, after the empty-selection skip and before any shard runs, and records it as top-level `summary[\"sandbox\"]`. `probe()` is `lru_cache`d and every base and head run in one invocation shares it, and CI runs one shard per invocation, so one value per summary names the mechanism for each shard's runs. `SandboxUnavailable` becomes `GateError(\"sandbox-unavailable\", <message naming sandbox-exec/bwrap>)`, so `main()` writes `summary.json` with that `failure_class`. Disposition: fatal for the run (exit 1, Verified -1), classified as runner infrastructure, not a mutation finding; it is fixed on the runner, not by recheck or code change.\n4. Docs: `docs/mutation-testing.md` (summary `sandbox` field, CI fails closed, `sandbox-unavailable` meaning) and `docs/local-dev-env.md` (CI sets no waiver).\n`evals/similar-tickets/digests.json` mentions the waiver name as eval corpus text and is deliberately left unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`: `mechanism()` returns the probed mechanism, returns `unsandboxed` under the waiver, raises without it.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`: (a) `run` with `probe` patched to `None` and no waiver exits 1 and writes `summary.json` with `failure_class == \"sandbox-unavailable\"` and a detail containing `bwrap`; (b) existing `run_gate` tests assert `summary[\"sandbox\"]`; (c) the string `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` appears nowhere in the raw text of `_mutation.yml`, `mutation.yml`, `test.yml` or `gerrit-verify.yaml` (covers workflow, job and step env and `$GITHUB_ENV` writes); (d) the gate job's `runs-on` is `ubuntu-26.04`.\n- `make verify` green before push.\n- Pre-merge Verified runs dispatch from `main`, so they use main's `_mutation.yml` and cannot prove the no-waiver lane. After merge, dispatch `Mutation Testing Sweep` (`mutation.yml`, all shards) on `main` and inspect a shard: step env has no waiver, log has no `UNSANDBOXED` line, published `summary.json` has `sandbox` = `bwrap`.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml`\n- `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py`, `scripts/mutation_gate.py`\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`, `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`\n- `docs/mutation-testing.md`, `docs/local-dev-env.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No workflow among `_mutation.yml`, `mutation.yml`, `test.yml`, `gerrit-verify.yaml` contains `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`, asserted by test (c).\n- [x] With no working sandbox and no waiver, `mutation_gate.py run` exits 1 and writes `summary.json` with `failure_class` `sandbox-unavailable` and a detail naming `bwrap`, asserted by test (a).\n- [x] `summary.json` records the sandbox mechanism under `sandbox`, asserted by test (b).\n- [x] A post-merge `Mutation Testing Sweep` dispatch on `main` shows shards with `sandbox` = `bwrap` in the published `summary.json` and no waiver in the log; run URL recorded on this ticket.\n- [x] `make verify` passes on the final patch set.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml","reason":"drop the unsandboxed waiver, pin ubuntu-26.04, fix stale comments"},{"path":".github/actionlint.yaml","reason":"declare the ubuntu-26.04 label that actionlint 1.7.12 does not know (rhysd/actionlint#682)"},{"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"add mechanism() and UNSANDBOXED"},{"path":"scripts/mutation_gate.py","reason":"record mechanism in summary; SandboxUnavailable -> GateError"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"mechanism() tests"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py","reason":"fail-closed summary, sandbox record, workflow waiver and runs-on tests"},{"path":"docs/mutation-testing.md","reason":"document CI fail-closed and summary field"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"document CI sets no waiver"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e5df-89bd-7e75-4031"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"fea1ad0b-0533-4760-b740-79ff7a25d163","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"248a-9e8d-afc3-4518","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mutation lane waives the sandbox unconditionally, so a runner where bwrap cannot start reports green as if sandboxed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["facfeedd-750c-45bd-b367-fad4b8b88e96","da0561e2-5016-4336-b611-4e414cbef6fd","705976a9-3028-4dc4-a041-94aa07e75263","656723d7-e138-4235-ac8d-3f50f434baa7","fea1ad0b-0533-4760-b740-79ff7a25d163","ad51e7cb-3405-4c02-9ace-c46b3e0b0ab9","784c6319-7233-4b03-9c90-feea148b3daa","1bb1a469-b465-49ed-9a8b-2d80d5fd4420","41acc9a2-bda0-49be-b84a-1a6f1957b69d","748466f6-ffd4-42cc-819e-70ea7bd789de","d0ba2583-992e-45e3-9ecd-a7a2cd0a32c6","f1be1f62-407c-4b5f-95f6-7c15f7afefec","c0cf2ca0-7808-40f6-a8f7-f7851ce9cccf","7cc077d7-488d-48f5-ba40-3a0e881d27e6","0f30d73f-2551-444a-bbbb-a32b40d95687"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794443861179355777,"uuid":"92bd1472-e093-4219-9760-6a689465aaaa"}